  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 166060244992
    m_Localized: Rules of the game
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 502774775808
    m_Localized: '* A random word from the built-in dictionary is placed in the center
      line of the board.

      * The player must drag one letter from the alphabet
      and place it in an empty cell on the board next to other letters to form a
      new word.

      * Then, they must sequentially select letters on the board
      to form the word and click the "Move" button.

      * Words cannot be repeated
      during a single game.

      * A word cannot contain the same letter on the
      board twice.

      * A word can be read in any direction except diagonally.

      *
      One point is awarded for each letter in the word.

      * The player must
      make a move within the allotted time.

      * If a player fails to make a
      move, they are awarded a pass.

      * If a player''s number of passes reaches
      the maximum, they are awarded a loss and the game ends (the number of points
      scored is not counted).

      * The game is also considered complete when
      all the board cells are filled with letters. * The player with the most points
      wins.

      * If the players have the same number of points, the game is declared
      a draw.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 20447734677504
    m_Localized: Questions and Answers
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 20937088319488
    m_Localized: "<b>How do I remove the highlighted letters on the board?</b>\r\n
      - Click the \"Clear\" button. This does not remove the letter from the board.\r\n\r\n<b>How
      do I remove a letter from the board?</b>\r\n - Click the \"Cancel\" button.
      This not only removes the letter from the board but also removes the highlight
      (if the letters were highlighted).\r\n\r\n<b>How do I pause the game?</b>\r\n
      - Click the \"Pause\" button. This stops the turn timer and hides the letters
      on the board for the duration of the pause.\r\n - To resume the game, click
      the \"Pause\" button again.\r\n\r\n<b>How do I exit a game if it's not finished
      yet?</b>\r\n - Click the \"Home\" button.\r\n - If you're playing with AI,
      a window will appear asking if you want to save the current game.\r\n --  If
      the game has been saved, you can load it later and continue playing from the
      saved point.\r\n\r\n<b>How do I use the \"Bukovka\" booster?</b>\r\n - Click
      the booster icon on the panel, if available. When activated, AI algorithms
      are used to search for a word (the longest possible), place a letter on the
      board, and highlight that word on the board.\r\n - If the AI \u200B\u200Bfails
      to find the word, the booster will be returned to the player's inventory.\r\n\r\n<b>How
      do I use the Slowdown booster?</b>\r\n - Click the booster icon on the panel
      if one is available.\r\n - When activated, it pauses the timer for a certain
      period (e.g., 30 seconds), giving the player additional time to make a move.\r\n\r\n<b>How
      do I purchase boosters?</b>\r\n - Boosters are always available for purchase
      in the in-game store for real money.\r\n - Boosters can also be obtained by
      watching ads."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
